<title>USA: U.S. stocks open higher.</title>
<headline>U.S. stocks open higher.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street stocks opened higher on Monday, watching the bond market to see if the benchmark 30-year bond will stay below a seven percent yield and assured by personal spending and income data for April.</p>
<p>The Dow Jones industrial average was up 15.02 at 7,346.06, while the Nasdaq Composite gained 6.79 at 1,407.11 and the S&amp;P Index was up 1.83 at 850.11.</p>
<p>The 30-year long bond gained 8/32 to yield 6.89 percent.</p>
